    \\\"comment_ref\\\": \\\"draft-3\\\",\n      \\\"persona_id\\\": \\\"persona-lina-kovac\\\",\n      \\\"body\\\": \\\"The self-truthmaking cases put pressure on any view that treats all grounding as explanation in the thick sense. If a proposition can make true its own existence claim, that may be a legitimate truthmaking relation, but it is hard to see it as answering a substantive why-question in the way the essence argument requires.\\\",\n      \\\"parent_ref\\\": null,\n      \\\"score_assessment\\\": {\n        \\\"score\\\": 21,\n        \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Accurately uses the reflexivity cases to test the explanatory adequacy standard from the necessity source.\\\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"comment_ref\\\": \\\"draft-4\\\",\n      \\\"persona_id\\\": \\\"persona-rory-chen\\\",\n      \\\"body\\\": \\\"There is also a possible defense of Trogdon here: if apparent counterexamples often involve partial grounds, omitted enablers, or misidentified grounds, then truthmaking counterexamples might show incompleteness rather than a failure of grounding necessity. The hard part is explaining why that response is not just screening off every awkward case.\\\",\n      \\\"parent_ref\\\": null,\n      \\\"score_assessment\\\": {\n        \\\"score\\\": 18,\n        \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reflects Trogdon's counterexample strategy while identifying a fair burden for applying it to truthmaking.\\\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"comment_ref\\\": \\\"draft-5\\\",\n      \\\"persona_id\\\": \\\"persona-samira-haddad\\\",\n      \\\"body\\\": \\\"Rodriguez-Pereyra's species strategy is strongest if truthmaking and alethic-fact grounding really are cases of grounding rather than merely nearby relations. Once that premise is accepted, the contrast with Trogdon becomes sharper: grounding may be unified enough to include truthmaking, but not uniform enough for every species to behave like full explanatory grounding.\\\",\n      \\\"parent_ref\\\": \\\"draft-3\